[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:41. Illusions of Pastoral Peace]
[00:00.360] Passage 41 | 文章41
[00:01.500] Illusions of pastoral peace. | 田园和平的幻想。
[00:05.105] The quiet life of the country has never appealed to me. | 乡村的宁静生活从未吸引过我。
[00:09.850] City-born and city-bred, I have always regarded the country as something you look at through a train window, | 生于城市、长于城市，我一直把乡村看作是透过火车窗户才能看到的东西，
[00:16.135] or something you occasionally visit during the weekend. | 或是周末偶尔去拜访的地方。
[00:19.640] Most of my friends live in the city. | 我的大多数朋友都住在城里。
[00:22.420] Yet they always go into raptures at the mere mention of the country. | 然而，他们一提到乡村就欣喜若狂。
[00:26.610] Though they extol the virtues of the peaceful life, | 尽管他们颂扬宁静生活的美德，
[00:29.720] only one of them has ever gone to live in the country, | 但只有一个人曾去乡村居住，
[00:32.745] and he was back in town within six months. | 并且他在六个月内就回城了。
[00:35.590] Even he still lives under the illusion that country life is somehow superior to town life. | 即使是他，仍然活在乡村生活某种程度上优于城市生活的幻觉中。
[00:41.885] He is forever talking about the friendly people, the clean atmosphere, | 他总是谈论着友善的人们，清新的空气，
[00:47.105] the closeness to nature and the gentle pace of living. | 亲近大自然以及悠闲的生活节奏。
[00:50.445] Nothing can be compared, he maintains, with the first cock crow, | 他坚持认为，没有什么能与第一声鸡鸣，
[00:54.885] the twittering of birds at dawn, | 黎明时鸟儿的啁啾，
[00:57.300] the sight of the rising sun glinting on the trees and pastures. | 以及旭日东升时在树木和牧场上闪耀的景象相比。
[01:01.355] This idyllic pastoral scene is only part of the picture. | 这田园诗般的乡村景象只是一部分。
[01:05.470] My friend fails to mention the long and friendless winter evenings, | 我的朋友没有提到漫长而孤寂的冬夜，
[01:09.785] which are interrupted only by an occasional visit to the local cinema, | 只有偶尔去当地电影院看电影才能打断，
[01:13.595] virtually the only form of entertainment. | 这几乎是唯一的娱乐方式。
[01:16.485] He says nothing about the poor selection of goods in the shops, | 他没有提到商店里商品选择的匮乏，
[01:20.600] or about those unfortunate people who have to travel from the country to the city every day to get to work. | 也没有提到那些不幸的人们，他们每天不得不从乡村前往城市上班。
[01:27.525] Why people are prepared to tolerate a four-hour journey each day | 为什么人们愿意每天忍受四小时的通勤，
[01:31.725] for the dubious privilege of living in the country is beyond my ken. | 以换取住在乡村这一可疑的特权，这超出了我的理解范围。
[01:36.250] They could be saved so much misery and expense if they chose to live in the city, where they rightly belong. | 如果他们选择住在他们本该居住的城市，就能省去许多痛苦和开销。
[01:43.380] If you can do without the few pastoral pleasures of the country, | 如果你能舍弃乡村的那些田园乐趣，
[01:47.685] you will find the city can provide you with the best that life can offer. | 你会发现城市能提供生活中最美好的东西。
[01:52.080] You never have to travel miles to see your friends. | 你从来不需要长途跋涉去看望朋友。
[01:55.700] They invariably live nearby, and are always available for an informal chat or an evening’s entertainment. | 他们总是住在附近，随时可以进行非正式聊天或晚间娱乐。
[02:02.655] Some of my acquaintances in the country come up to town once or twice a year | 我在乡村的一些熟人一年来城里一两次，
[02:06.895] to visit the theatre as a special treat. | 作为一种特殊的款待去剧院。
[02:09.505] For them, this is a major operation, which involves considerable planning. | 对他们来说，这是一项大工程，需要周密的计划。
[02:15.010] As the play draws to its close, they wonder whether they will ever catch that last train home. | 当戏剧接近尾声时，他们会担心能否赶上回家的末班车。
[02:20.885] The city dweller never experiences anxieties of this sort. | 城市居民从不会经历这种焦虑。
[02:25.340] The latest exhibitions, films or plays are only a short bus ride away. | 最新的展览、电影或戏剧都只需乘坐短途巴士即可到达。
[02:30.950] Shopping, too, is always a pleasure. | 购物也总是令人愉快的。
[02:33.980] There is so much variety that you never have to make do with second best. | 商品种类繁多，你永远不必将就次等货。
[02:38.875] Country people run wild when they go shopping in the city, | 乡下人进城购物时会变得疯狂，
[02:43.025] and stagger home loaded with as many of the necessities of life as they can carry. | 然后蹒跚地回到家，满载着他们能拿的尽可能多的生活必需品。
[02:48.470] Nor is the city without its moments of beauty. | 城市也并非没有它的美丽时刻。
[02:52.265] There is something comforting about the warm glow shed by advertisements on cold, wet winter nights. | 在寒冷潮湿的冬夜里，广告牌散发出的温暖光芒总能给人带来慰藉。
[02:59.600] Few things could be more impressive than the peace that descends on deserted city streets at weekends, | 在周末，当那些每天通勤数千人的城市街道变得空无一人时，那种宁静是如此令人印象深刻。
[03:06.415] when the thousands that travel to work every day are tucked away in their homes in the country. | 数千名每天上班的人都回到了他们在乡村的家中。
[03:12.090] It has always been a mystery to me why city dwellers, who appreciate all these things, | 对我来说，这始终是一个谜，为什么那些欣赏所有这些的城市居民，
[03:18.810] obstinately pretend that they would prefer to live in the country. | 却固执地假装他们宁愿住在乡村。